@participant13 if a TPM used to work on this machine but then broke/disappeared, then this failure is expected. From participant20 client's perspective, this looks like the state file got copied to another machine without a TPM, which is what this feature specifically tries to prevent.

If your machine cannot have a TPM reliably working, I recommend passing `--encrypt-state=false` to `tailscaled` via `/etc/defaults/tailscaled`.
I get that this might be a frustrating response, like "works on my machine", but we are trying to prevent some very realistic attacks on users (exfiltration of state files from legit machines by attackers). This just doesn't work if a TPM randomly disappears on an existing node.

